= Handling This Cartridge

This cartridge is for the Sega Genesis and Mega Drive systems only. It carries a MegaWiFi Rev.C
board, a small Wi-Fi computer that brings live air traffic to your console.

- Always turn the power switch *OFF* before inserting or removing the cartridge.
- Do not bend it, crush it, drop it or get it wet.
- Keep it out of direct sunlight and away from heaters and other heat sources.
- Do not touch the metal contacts at the bottom of the cartridge.
- The USB-C port on the cartridge is for updating its Wi-Fi firmware. You don't need it to play.
- Take a 10 to 15 minute break every hour or so, even if you don't think you need it.

== Warning: read before using your Genesis

A very small number of people have epileptic seizures when they see certain patterns or flashing
lights, including some patterns on a television screen. If you or anyone in your family has
epilepsy, ask your doctor before using a video game system. If you feel dizzy, see blurred
vision, have eye or muscle twitches, lose awareness, feel disoriented or make any involuntary
movement while playing, *stop immediately* and see your doctor.

== Owners of projection and plasma televisions

A still picture shown for a long time can leave a permanent image on some projection, plasma and
older tube screens. The radar's rings, side panel and labels never move, so don't leave it running
for hours on a screen that can burn in. LCD screens are not affected.

#note[Not for navigation][The radar shows public ADS-B reports, which can be late, incomplete or
wrong. It is a toy. Never use it to make decisions about real aircraft.]
